---
import PageLayout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import siteConfig from '~/config/site';

const updated = '2026-11-19';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Terms"
  heading="Terms of use"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  intro="Rules for using this site, and what the content is not."
  description={`Terms of use for ${siteConfig.name}.`}
  crumbs={[{ label: 'Terms' }]}
>
  <section class="wrap sec" style="padding-top:0">
    <div class="prose rev">
      <p>Last updated: {updated}</p>

      <h2>What the content is</h2>
      <p>
        Articles and notes here are general information. They are
        <strong>not legal advice on any specific matter</strong>. Reading them does not
        create a lawyer–client relationship.
      </p>

      <h2>Specific matters</h2>
      <p>
        Outcomes depend on facts, evidence, procedure and the local tribunal. For a real
        matter, engage formally rather than relying on what is published here.
      </p>

      <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        Original text and images belong to the author. Quoting with attribution and a link
        is welcome. Republishing whole pages, or reusing content in misleading or commercial
        training material, is not.
      </p>

      <h2>External links</h2>
      <p>
        Links to statutes, judgments or other sites do not imply endorsement. Accuracy and
        currency are the responsibility of the source.
      </p>

      <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        Content is kept as accurate and current as practical, but no liability is accepted
        for loss arising from its use. Where the law changes, the version in force applies.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this site:
        <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contact.email}`}>{siteConfig.contact.email}</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</PageLayout>
